{%- comment -%}
  fye-carat-label — format a carat weight for display.

  Built 01/09/2026, W916. One rule, one place: the stepper prints three of
  these per page (smaller, current, larger) and they must agree.

  THE RULE: trim trailing zeros, never pad.

      0.50  ->  0.5
      1.00  ->  1
      1.5   ->  1.5
      0.33  ->  0.33

  Liquid renders a decimal's own string form, so 1.0 prints as "1.0" and
  0.50 as "0.5" — the first is wrong and the second is right, which is why
  this cannot just be `{{ value }}`. A whole number is emitted as an integer;
  anything else is rounded to two places, which Ruby already renders without
  trailing zeros.

  ZERO AND NIL BOTH RENDER NOTHING. Added 01/09/2026 after the stepper showed
  "0ct" on every control: `nil == blank` is true in Liquid but `0 == blank` is
  FALSE, so an unwritten or zeroed metafield printed a real-looking weight. No
  ring weighs nothing, so zero can only mean missing data — and a wrong number
  is worse than no number, because the shopper cannot tell it is wrong.

  Callers therefore test the captured string for emptiness rather than
  repeating this guard.

  Parameters:
    value — a number
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign n = value | plus: 0
  assign whole = n | floor
-%}
{%- if value == blank -%}
{%- elsif n <= 0 -%}
{%- elsif n == whole -%}{{ whole }}
{%- else -%}{{ n | round: 2 }}
{%- endif -%}
